Including full stack traces in error responses can expose sensitive information like file paths, internal system details, and application structure to clients. Consider only including stack traces in development/debug mode or sanitizing them before sending to clients.
```suggestion
        let message: string;
        if (
          (typeof process !== "undefined" && process.env.NODE_ENV === "development") ||
          (typeof Bun !== "undefined" && Bun.env.NODE_ENV === "development")
        ) {
          message = err instanceof Error && err.stack ? err.stack : err.toString();
        } else {
          message = err instanceof Error ? err.message : "An unexpected error occurred";
        }
```

